<p>In the latest development, Hezbollah leader Naim Qassem said the group would not enter negotiations with Israel while Israeli attacks continue, calling talks under fire a form of surrender. The statement came as Israel kept up strikes in Lebanon, including around Beirut’s southern suburbs and the south, while also issuing new evacuation warnings and saying it was expanding a security buffer inside Lebanese territory. The renewed exchanges underscore that neither side is showing signs of stepping back for now. The fighting traces back to the wider regional war, with Hezbollah having begun firing rockets into Israel and Israel saying it sent ground troops to take control of a strip in southern Lebanon up to the Litani River, about 30 kilometers from the border. Lebanese leaders have meanwhile called for direct negotiations, but Hezbollah publicly rejected that path in the current circumstances.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/KYoLs0ymAR0bBv_7ZTWwr7Yvt4WS320BVSMQeD3HUSi9PYkoyMVVH6J6_dH17KDxA2jmWNQuqKlYlhAhlYe9Kc2t0RM9GvzaJR8ud9ksh-Y58Yf7nQvNMTDLKinwDiRnzSTMrDjl_uspwpAdobGqJ7mA_jw2GhZNFq9ZJBxlip-HbmPr2fF1EhoQV29T2CglQGv6OaFM1Bz9GsIA' alt='An Israeli strike in Qlaileh in southern Lebanon on Wednesday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Cross-border claims: Le Monde reported that Hezbollah said it attacked Israeli troops inside Lebanon as well as targets in northern Israel during the same round of escalation.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Hezbollah: Naim Qassem said the group sees negotiations during ongoing Israeli attacks as surrender and signaled it will continue resisting under current conditions. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/hezbollah-rejects-truce-talks-israel-presses-lebanon-strikes'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>Israel: Israeli officials framed the military push as an expansion of a buffer zone in southern Lebanon. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/25/world/middleeast/israel-lebanon-hezbollah.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Lebanese presidency: President Joseph Aoun urged direct negotiations with Israel, a position Hezbollah rejected in public remarks. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/25/war-in-lebanon-hezbollah-says-negotiating-with-israel-would-be-surrender_6751812_4.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/hezbollah-rejects-truce-talks-israel-presses-lebanon-strikes'>Hezbollah rejects truce talks as Israel presses Lebanon strikes</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/hezbollah-says-negotiating-with-israel-would-be-surrender-amid-strikes-on-lebanon'>Hezbollah says negotiating with Israel would be surrender, amid strikes on Lebanon</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/25/war-in-lebanon-hezbollah-says-negotiating-with-israel-would-be-surrender_6751812_4.html'>War in Lebanon: Hezbollah says negotiating with Israel would be surrender</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/25/world/middleeast/israel-lebanon-hezbollah.html'>Israel Keeps Up Strikes in Lebanon as Hezbollah Signals Defiance</a> - nytimes.com</li></ul>